    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20166" root="سك" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَرَبُوا بُيُوتَهُمْ سِكَاكًا</span></b>  [<i>They pitched their tents</i>]
<i>in one row:</i> (Th, K:) and said with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ش</span>, [i. e.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِكَاكًا</span>,] accord. to IAar: (TA:) but Th says
that it is only with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">س</span>, deriving it from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِكَّةٌ</span> signifying “a wide <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُقَاق</span>.” (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شك</span>.)

